# Copy this file to `.env.local` and paste your key there. `.env.local` is
# gitignored; this file is not, so never put a real key in here.
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Get a key from https://platform.decart.ai/ . New accounts come with free
# trial credits — use those before spending (PRD §7).

# --- Local development only ------------------------------------------------
# Vite INLINES every `VITE_`-prefixed variable into the built JavaScript, so a
# key set here would normally end up in plain text inside `dist/`.
#
# It doesn't, because `resolveApiKey()` in src/lucy.ts reads this behind an
# `import.meta.env.DEV` guard. Vite compiles that to `false` for a production
# build and drops the branch, key literal and all — verified by grepping the
# built bundle. So `npm run dev` sees this value and `npm run build` cannot.
#
# The upshot: this is a dev-only convenience and a deployed build genuinely
# cannot carry it. Real users enter their own key in the UI, which is kept in
# localStorage (PRD Phase 2, "BYO key"). Leave this blank to test that path.
VITE_DECART_API_KEY=
